{# ── Chapter: Takeaway ── #}
<section class="case-chapter" data-chapter="takeaway">
  <h2>Remember</h2>
  <div class="case-takeaway">
    <h3>Key takeaways</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <div class="tone-junior">localStorage.setItem() can throw once its quota is full, and the throw is real, not silent truncation — wrap writes in try/catch or a long enough session will eventually hit an uncaught error.</div>
        <div class="tone-mid">Give every write a real fallback: evict the oldest entries, cap what's stored, or fall back to in-memory for that session — don't just catch and ignore the error.</div>
        <div class="tone-staff">localStorage isn't cleared by a user's "clear cookies" flow and can be partitioned per top-level site or quota-zeroed in private browsing — treat every write as fallible by construction, and never store data a user would expect to vanish with their cookies.</div>
      </li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>
